## 4. `dim_relationship_slicer`

Maps the three filter options to sets of `relationship` values in the fact table.

```dax
dim_relationship_slicer =
DATATABLE(
    "RelKey",    STRING,
    "RelLabel",  STRING,
    "SortOrder", INTEGER,
    {
        { "ALL",              "All Relationships",  1 },
        { "INTIMATE_PARTNER", "Intimate Partner",   2 },
        { "FAMILY",           "Family",             3 }
    }
)
```

Slicer config: field = `RelLabel`, sort by `SortOrder`, **single-select**.

Relationship values mapped internally in every measure (see §5):

| RelKey | Includes these `relationship` values |
|---|---|
| `INTIMATE_PARTNER` | Victim Was Spouse · Victim Was Common-Law Spouse · Victim was Ex-Spouse · Victim Was Ex-Relationship (Ex-Boyfriend/Girlfriend) · Victim Was Boyfriend/Girlfriend |
| `FAMILY` | Victim Was Child · Victim Was Child of Boyfriend or Girlfriend · Victim Was Parent · Victim Was Stepchild · Victim Was Stepparent · Victim was Foster Parent |
| `ALL` | No relationship filter applied |

Note the case inconsistency in source data: "Victim **was** Ex-Spouse" and "Victim **was** Foster Parent" use lowercase "was." Both forms are included in the IN lists below.

